NAME
     date - print or set the time

SYNOPSIS
     date [+FORMAT]
     date -s STRING

DESCRIPTION
     date prints the time of day. With a +FORMAT it prints it that way:
     %Y %m %d %H %M %S %j %a %A %b %B %Z %s and the rest of the usual
     letters. With -s it sets the clock, which is root's alone.

OPTIONS
     -s STRING   set the clock from STRING

SEE ALSO
     cal(1), uptime(1), touch(1)
